body:
Avoids messy conditionals

```c++
switch(choice){
	case 1:
		// do stuff;
		// break;
	case 2:
		// do other stuff;
		// break;
	case 'y':
		// ...;
		// break;
}
```

Without including break it prints all cases below until a break is found, sometimes thats useful. For that same reason, **Cases don't need curcly braces.**
ex:
```C++
switch(choice){
	case 'y':
	case 'Y':
		cout << "yes";
		count << endl;
		// Notice you don't need {}
		break;
	case 'n':
	case 'N':
		cout << "no";
		count << endl;
		break;
}
```
	Basically acting as if ('y' or 'Y')...
